Window and taskbar perching (Phase 4)
`````````````````````````````````````

| Upstream path | Local path | Modifications |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `Assets/MATE ENGINE - Scripts/Settings/MonitorHelper.cs` | `unity/WaifuAvatar/Assets/WaifuAvatar/Scripts/Window/MonitorGeometry.cs`, `.../Window/DesktopWindows.cs` | Split the taskbar-edge derivation (monitor rect minus work area) from its P/Invoke so it can be unit tested. Return which edge the taskbar occupies instead of only its rect, and allow perching only on a bottom-docked taskbar. Added a full-screen-coverage test. `GetScaleForWindow` became `DesktopWindows.GetScale`. |
| `Assets/MATE ENGINE - Scripts/AvatarHandlers/AvatarWindowHandler.cs` | `.../Window/WindowSitPolicy.cs`, `.../Window/DesktopWindows.cs`, `.../Window/WindowSitter.cs` | Split one ~1000-line MonoBehaviour into a scene-free policy class, a Windows-only enumeration layer, and a thin glue component. Kept the snap/unsnap safeguards (drag hold time, drag distance, probe radius, latch ticks, unsnap cooldown, guard zone, cursor-delta unsnap) and the invisible-window filters (layered/click-through/tool/no-activate/colour-key/low-alpha, cloaked, shell classes, owned windows). Replaced the seat-anchor bisection and one-frame recalibration with a settle window that measures the live seat offset then freezes it. Dropped the depth-only occluder quads entirely. Replaced Animator bool parameters with VRMA clip requests. Folded the taskbar in as one more candidate rather than a separate code path. |
| `Assets/MATE ENGINE - Scripts/AvatarHandlers/AvatarTaskbarController.cs` | `.../Window/MonitorGeometry.cs`, `.../Window/WindowSitter.cs` | Absorbed into the same candidate list as ordinary windows. Uses the monitor/work-area difference instead of `SHAppBarMessage(ABM_GETTASKBARPOS)`, which reports a rect even when the taskbar is auto-hidden. Dropped the bone-attachment and spawn/despawn scaling, which served a Mate-Engine prop feature this project does not have. |

Drag inertia (sway)
```````````````````

| Upstream path | Local path | Modifications |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `Assets/MATE ENGINE - Scripts/AvatarHandlers/AvatarSwayController.cs` | `unity/WaifuAvatar/Assets/WaifuAvatar/Scripts/Avatar/SwayModel.cs` | Kept the signal chain (window velocity, low-pass filter, spring, opposite-phase limb lag, asymmetric weight fade, clamped lean) and the lean/limb limits. Converted the input from pixels-per-frame to pixels-per-second so the same gesture leans the same amount at any frame rate. Replaced the explicit-Euler spring with this project's implicit-Euler `Spring`, which does not diverge when the frame delta spikes. Removed the direct `localRotation` writes and inverse-quaternion cleanup: `PoseOverlay` already owns additive-overlay bookkeeping, so this class only produces angles. Dropped the animator-state whitelist, the global/local rotation-space switch, and the invert toggles, none of which this project exposes. |

Within-monitor roaming
``````````````````````

| Upstream path | Local path | Modifications |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `Assets/MATE ENGINE - Scripts/AvatarHandlers/AvatarLocomotionController.cs` | `unity/WaifuAvatar/Assets/WaifuAvatar/Scripts/Window/RoamPlanner.cs`, `.../Window/Roamer.cs` | Kept the three rules that matter: walk only while in base idle and stop immediately otherwise; measure screen edges against the avatar's rendered silhouette rather than the transparent window rect; turn away when close to an edge. Split the decision rules into a scene-free planner with an injectable RNG. Replaced the uniform-random walk interval with an exponential dwell and a floor, matching this project's animation-statistics rule. Added cursor avoidance (asymmetric, so an avatar already beside the cursor can still walk away from it) and clamped the planned distance to the remaining room so the avatar cannot march into a wall. Walk within the work area rather than the full virtual screen, so it does not cover the taskbar. Dropped the Steam/animator-parameter wiring, the debug GUI overlay, and the multi-monitor traversal — cross-monitor movement already exists in `src/main/roaming.ts`. |

Desktop ambient light
`````````````````````

| Upstream path | Local path | Modifications |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `Assets/MATE ENGINE - Scripts/Tools/DesktopAmbientProbe.cs` | `unity/WaifuAvatar/Assets/WaifuAvatar/Scripts/Avatar/AmbientMix.cs`, `.../Window/DesktopAmbient.cs`, `.../Window/AmbientLights.cs` | Kept the two colour decisions that matter: discard sampled value and derive light intensity from saturation, so a dark desktop dims the light instead of blacking it out; and damp hue the short way around the colour wheel so a red-to-orange change does not sweep through green and blue. Kept the downscaled `StretchBlt` capture, the four edge bands, and excluding the avatar's own window from the average. Split the colour maths into a scene-free class. Damp every frame rather than only on capture frames, so the light does not step at the sample rate. Return mid-grey rather than black when the avatar covers a whole band. Skip capture entirely when no lights are wired up. Default off, with the capture behaviour spelled out in the settings screen. |

